# Osseous Exhale without a Dragon: Bot1 has no Dragon to choose and none in hand, so an attempted behold payment rolls back (CR 701.4a, 733) and no life
# is gained. It targets a blocking creature (CR 506.3): Bot1 attacks with Memnite on turn 3, Bot2's Ornithopter blocks, and the
# Ornithopter takes 5 and dies. Bot2's idle Memnite and Bot2 itself are no legal targets.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Mox Ruby
Memnite
Osseous Exhale
Plains x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Memnite
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Memnite.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Memnite.Cast
[T3 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(Memnite > Bot2)
[T3 Bot1.DeclareBlockers]
Bot2.Block(Ornithopter > Memnite)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Osseous Exhale.Cast
Bot1.Modes(Behold a Dragon)
Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
? Stack.Count = 0
? Bot1.Mana = {W}{R}
? Bot1.Graveyard.Count = 0
? Bot1.Life = 20
? Bot1.Revealed = (absent)
Bot1.Hand.Osseous Exhale.Cast
Bot1.Modes(Cast without beholding)
! Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Memnite)
! Bot1.Target(Bot2)
Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 20
Bot1.Revealed = (absent)
Bot2.Graveyard = Ornithopter
Bot2.Battlefield = Memnite
